WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.828
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:15.182
Unit twenty-two: Famous People. In this unit, you will talk about famous people's lives.

4
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:16.964
Famous.

5
00:00:17.664 --> 00:00:19.896
Famous means known by very many people.

6
00:00:20.196 --> 00:00:21.591
She is a famous singer.

7
00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:25.118
Your turn. Say: Famous.

8
00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:28.691
Famous.

9
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:30.487
Singer.

10
00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:35.079
Singer means a person who sings, often as a job.

11
00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:37.750
Sinn Sisamouth was a famous Khmer singer.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.265
Your turn. Say: Singer.

13
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:44.838
Singer.

14
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.723
Athlete.

15
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:49.829
Athlete means a person who is good at sports.

16
00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:52.187
The athlete ran very fast.

17
00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:55.203
Your turn. Say: Athlete.

18
00:00:57.903 --> 00:00:58.846
Athlete.

19
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.932
Scientist.

20
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:04.061
Scientist means a person who studies science.

21
00:01:04.361 --> 00:01:06.547
Marie Curie was a great scientist.

22
00:01:07.247 --> 00:01:09.609
Your turn. Say: Scientist.

23
00:01:12.309 --> 00:01:13.414
Scientist.

24
00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:15.139
Born.

25
00:01:15.839 --> 00:01:17.839
Born means when you started your life.

26
00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:19.999
She was born in 1990.

27
00:01:20.699 --> 00:01:22.980
Your turn. Say: Born.

28
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.332
Born.

29
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:28.004
Won.

30
00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:30.332
Won means past of win.

31
00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:31.958
He won a gold medal.

32
00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:34.579
Your turn. Say: Won.

33
00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:38.037
Won.

34
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:39.830
Became.

35
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.285
Became means past of become: started to be.

36
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:44.969
She became a doctor.

37
00:01:45.669 --> 00:01:48.461
Your turn. Say: Became.

38
00:01:51.161 --> 00:01:52.046
Became.

39
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.098
Inspire.

40
00:01:54.798 --> 00:01:57.772
Inspire means to give someone the wish to do something good.

41
00:01:58.072 --> 00:02:00.060
Famous people can inspire us.

42
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.995
Your turn. Say: Inspire.

43
00:02:05.695 --> 00:02:06.823
Inspire.

44
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:09.758
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:10.058 --> 00:02:12.917
Sreypich, which famous person inspires you?

46
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:16.811
Marie Curie. She was a great scientist.

47
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:19.245
When was she born?

48
00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.326
She was born in 1867 in Poland.

49
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:26.757
What did she do?

50
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.642
She became the first woman to win a Nobel Prize.

51
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.227
Grammar focus: Past simple (was born and became).

52
00:02:35.527 --> 00:02:39.328
She was born in 1990. He became a doctor.

53
00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:43.427
Always use 'was born' (not 'is born') to talk about the day someone's life started.

54
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:47.278
Now read and listen. People Who Inspire Us.

55
00:02:47.578 --> 00:02:49.752
Many famous people inspire us.

56
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.116
Marie Curie was born in Poland in 1867.

57
00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:59.264
She became a scientist and won two Nobel Prizes.

58
00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:04.001
A singer can move people with music, and an athlete can win medals.

59
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:08.547
Their stories show us that hard work can change the world.

60
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.340
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.081
She blank born in 1990.

62
00:03:15.381 --> 00:03:18.349
A, was. B, is. C, were.

63
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.175
The answer is A: was.

64
00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:27.311
He blank a famous athlete.

65
00:03:27.611 --> 00:03:32.356
A, became. B, becomed. C, become.

66
00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.048
The answer is A: became.

67
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.793
A person who is good at sports is an blank.

68
00:03:42.093 --> 00:03:45.538
A, athlete. B, singer. C, scientist.

69
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.608
The answer is A: athlete.

70
00:03:53.117 --> 00:03:57.641
Now it's your turn to speak. Which famous person inspires you? Why?

71
00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:08.670
Sinn Sisamouth inspires me. He was born in Stung Treng and became Cambodia's most famous singer.

72
00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.633
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:16.405
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past simple (was born and became).

74
00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:20.832
Today's value is inspiration. Learn from great people and follow your dreams.

75
00:04:21.132 --> 00:04:24.423
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

76
00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:28.118
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

